  "interpretation": "Illustrative configuration and callable roles, not an executed biological workflow. Panel A contrasts a site stack supplied with tile positions for stitching and a Z stack forming a volume. Other acquisition coordinates stay fixed within each stack; processing groups do not define its stack axis. Panels B and C show separate composition examples: group-specific chains and an artifact routed between steps within a compatible execution group. Sequential timepoints run the entire pipeline; wells can execute in parallel. Backend compatibility belongs to each callable contract."
